Builder Design Pattern

Suppose you have a class with many fields:

User user = new User(
    "Akhila",
    27,
    "Hyderabad",
    "abc@gmail.com",
    "9999999999",
    true
);

This becomes difficult to understand.

Which value represents what?

Also, what if some fields are optional?

Builder solves this.

User class
class User {

    private String name;
    private int age;
    private String city;
    private String email;

    private User(Builder builder) {
        this.name = builder.name;
        this.age = builder.age;
        this.city = builder.city;
        this.email = builder.email;
    }

    public static class Builder {

        private String name;
        private int age;
        private String city;
        private String email;

        public Builder name(String name) {
            this.name = name;
            return this;
        }

        public Builder age(int age) {
            this.age = age;
            return this;
        }

        public Builder city(String city) {
            this.city = city;
            return this;
        }

        public Builder email(String email) {
            this.email = email;
            return this;
        }

        public User build() {
            return new User(this);
        }
    }
}

Now creating the object becomes:

User user = new User.Builder()
        .name("Akhila")
        .age(27)
        .city("Hyderabad")
        .email("abc@gmail.com")
        .build();

Much easier to read.

Why is this called Builder?
Because you're building the object step by step.

Builder
   ↓
name()
   ↓
age()
   ↓
city()
   ↓
email()
   ↓
build()
   ↓
User object
Real-world Java example

You've probably seen:

StringBuilder builder = new StringBuilder();

builder.append("Hello")
       .append(" ")
       .append("World");

And in Spring/Java applications, Lombok can generate builder APIs:

@Builder
public class User {
    private String name;
    private int age;
    private String city;
}

Then:

User user = User.builder()
        .name("Akhila")
        .age(27)
        .city("Hyderabad")
        .build();
Easy way to remember

Builder = Create a complex object step by step.

🔥 All 6 patterns together

This is the part I want you to memorize for interviews:

| Pattern              | Main purpose              | Easy memory                     |
| -------------------- | ------------------------- | ------------------------------- |
| **Singleton**        | One instance              | **Only ONE**                    |
| **Factory**          | Create an object          | **Give me ONE type**            |
| **Abstract Factory** | Create related objects    | **Give me a FAMILY**            |
| **Observer**         | Notify multiple objects   | **One changes → MANY notified** |
| **Strategy**         | Select behavior/algorithm | **Choose behavior**             |
| **Builder**          | Construct complex object  | **Build step-by-step**          |

And their categories:
CREATIONAL
│
├── Singleton
├── Factory
├── Abstract Factory
└── Builder

BEHAVIORAL
│
├── Observer
└── Strategy
